            <ArticleTitle>Common pain scenarios.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>31-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Vertebral fractures and fibromyalgia, while very different and unrelated clinical conditions, are common pain conditions that can, at times, be difficult to diagnose and manage.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To discuss the investigation and treatment of two common pain conditions.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DISCUSSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Following a structured program for assessment and treatment, most people with both of these conditions can experience substantial improvement in the quality of their life.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
